            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "N_Rose P"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I give it 3 stars as it, however, it is easy to make and easy to adjust. What I did was substitute an equivicant amount of tropical fruit blend for the coconut, walnuts, and bananas and it was fantastic! 5-stars all the way! I've tried other combinations also, fresh berries with a berry juice blend, etc. The choices are only limited by your imagination. I've made it 3 or 4 times.",
            "datePublished": "2016-05-30T16:18:11.890Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "It's A New Day"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I don't have pineapple orange juice blend but I have pineapple juice and orange juice so I measured 2/3 cup of the two of them together (it was mostly pineapple juice). I also used up bits and pieces of various milks in the refrigerator to make a total of 4 cups of liquid. I used evaporated milk, reduced fat half and half and skim milk. I added the banana cut into cubes, not sliced. I really wanted to mash it but I didn't. I added a dribble of both coconut extract and rum extract. It froze up beautifully and is now in the freezer. My taste of what I scraped out of the ice cream maker was very good.",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-15T10:52:42.470Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kaithigg"
            },
            "reviewBody": "i made this just after i got my wisdom teeth out so i made some alterations. I also only had 1 cup of heavy cream and do not like pineapples.\n\n1 cup whipping cream\n1 1/4 cups 2% milk\n4 tbsp coconut milk powder\n1/2 pkg lemon pie filling\n3/4 cup sugar\n3 mashed bananas\n\nif i wasn't on a soft-food-only died, i would have used less coconut powder and added the flaked coconut and walnut pieces. I was scared the frozen banana slices would be too hard, so i mashed them, however i will probably just slice them the next time i make this recipe.\n\nI'm giving this 3 stars as it gave me a good start, however i made quite a few alterations to the recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2011-05-18T08:49:07.130Z"
          },
